    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `frai` CLI was consuming the `--ci` flag at its own option-parsing level and not forwarding it to the `frai-gate` CLI. The `frai-gate` command was only receiving the positional arguments (`['init']`), missing the flags.\n\n**The Fix:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` lines 753-755 to reconstruct the full command-line arguments from `process.argv`. This ensures all flags (including `--ci`) are properly forwarded to the `frai-gate` CLI:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : (args ?? []);\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` \u2192 Creates both FRAI-SPEC.md and .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init` \u2192 Creates only FRAI-SPEC.md (default behavior preserved)",
